    "body": "One defect in the stream operators of the card file model, found while comparing the output of `UseCase1_ExplicitSelectionAid` with its Java counterpart on the same card.\n\n### Commit\n\n- `61d0730` **render the elementary file content instead of addresses.** The `ElementaryFile` stream operator passed its SFI to the stream as a `uint8_t`, so a value such as 07h came out as an unprintable control character, and handed its header and data `shared_ptr` members straight to the stream, which rendered pointer addresses. `FileData` and `FileHeader` had no stream operator at all.\n\n`FileData` and `FileHeader` now render their records and their fields. The SFI is formatted in hexadecimal through a local `ostringstream`, so the caller's stream flags are left untouched. The header is omitted when null, since `FileHeader` is an incomplete type at that point.\n\n### Before and after\n\nThe C++ example printed a control character followed by two addresses, where the Java example printed:\n\n```\n{\"sfi\":\"07\",\"data\":{\"records\":{\"01\":\"010000000117041F82...\"}}}\n```\n\nThe C++ output now carries the same information.\n\n### Validation\n\nValidated on hardware with a Calypso card, comparing the rendered files of `UseCase1_ExplicitSelectionAid` against the Java example output on the same card.\n",
